Dear Micro X-Ray Sales and Applications Team,

I am working at INFN Laboratori Nazionali di Frascati, Rome, Italy, 
developing a laboratory fluorescence XAS instrument for measurements 
above 20 keV.

We currently have the following equipment:

Existing X-ray tube:
- Micro X-Ray Packaged X-Ray Tube
- 60 kV maximum voltage
- 75 W maximum power
- 1.7 A filament current
- 2 mA maximum anode current
- 25° beam angle
- Mo target

Existing power supply:
- Spellman uXHP65P100
- positive polarity, grounded-cathode architecture
- 65 kV maximum voltage
- 5 mA maximum current setpoint
- 100 W maximum power
- filament supply 0.3–3.5 A, 5 V maximum

We would like to request a quotation for a tube with:

- Packaged X-Ray Tube;
- tungsten target;
- 60 kV, 75 W continuous operation;
- 2.0 A filament version;
- approximately 50 µm focal spot;
- quotation for both 25° and 40° beam-angle configurations, if 
available;
- full compatibility with our existing Spellman uXHP65P100;
- HV cable and filament wiring included;

Our tube budget ceiling is EUR 30,000. We would need a complete 
quotation by 31 July 2026, valid for at least 90 days.

Photographs of our existing tube and power supply can be provided 
immediately.

Best regards,

